WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.633
The Moon.

00:02.333 --> 00:08.542
The Moon rises about fifty minutes later each night, so it is not always in the evening sky.

00:08.992 --> 00:13.791
When it is, point any binoculars at the line between its light and its dark.

00:14.241 --> 00:18.423
That is where the mountains and craters throw their longest shadows.
